I'll start by exploring the workspace and understanding the data before implementing the analysis.

```json
{
  "tool": "list_files",
  "args": {}
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/load_15min.csv"
  }
}
```

Let me check the data file first:
```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "head -50 data/load_15min.csv"
  }
}
```

Let me check the data more thoroughly using Python:
```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "python -c \"import pandas as pd; df = pd.read_csv('data/load_15min.csv'); print('Shape:', df.shape); print('Columns:', df.columns.tolist()); print('Date range:', df['timestamp_utc'].min(), 'to', df['timestamp_utc'].max()); print('Missing values:', df['load_mw'].isna().sum()); print(df.head(10))\""
  }
}
```

Now I have a good understanding of the data. Let me set up the workspace and create the analysis code:
```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "mkdir -p code outputs report/images"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "python -c \"import pandas as pd; df = pd.read_csv('data/load_15min.csv'); df['timestamp_utc'] = pd.to_datetime(df['timestamp_utc']); print('Missing by day:'); print(df[df['load_mw'].isna()].groupby(df[df['load_mw'].isna()]['timestamp_utc'].dt.date).size()); print('Stats:'); print(df['load_mw'].describe())\""
  }
}
```

Now let's run the analysis:
```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd /d F:\\Aworks\\1readraft\\ai_scientist\\meta_runs\\new_anthropic_claude-sonnet-4.6_no-reviewer\\round_001\\inner_workspaces\\round_001\\08b_EnergySystems_LoadForecastCSV && python code/analysis.py"
  }
}
```

Let me verify all files are in place and the report looks complete:
```json
{
  "tool": "list_files",
  "args": {}
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir report\\images\\"
  }
}
```

All deliverables are complete. Let me do a final check on the report:
```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "report/report.md"
  }
}
```
